{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["And the sense of <b>to YHWH who appeared to him</b> is that he gave thanks to the honored Name and offered Him a thanksgiving offering because He had appeared to him, for until now HaShem had not appeared to him nor made Himself known to him in a vision or in a spectacle, but rather it was said to him, \"Go forth from your land,\" in a dream of the night or by the holy spirit. And it is possible that \"who appeared to him\" alludes to the secret of the sacrifice (see Recanati 22a), and the enlightened will understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reference to Recanati appears to be a later editor's annotation, not Ramban's own words, but is translated as it stands in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:38.769079688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}